Z||000004||Spiff||09-24-2001||10:38 AM||||I saw the same Fiero with the offensive sticker also. Was it at the POCI show on Sunday? It's just what the young kids think is cool now. Don't let it get you mad. I didn't get to meet you at the show , but hope to meet more people at more shows. Don't let this persons stupid sticker get you mad. By the way I had the White 88 Formula T-Top.||||reg||1
Z||000005||frontal lobe||09-24-2001||10:52 AM||||I'm not against the person's right to use his/her freedom of speech, but accept that he/she might use it to be mean and thoughtless.  If, indeed, a "fat chick" really needed a ride, but WOULD cause a Fiero to scrape, I think many of us would be as careful as possible, but give the "fat chick" a ride anyway.<P>I suppose you could make a bumper sticker that said, "No fat DUDES, car will scrape", but that wouldn't really solve the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Voytek||09-24-2001||11:05 AM||||First define 'fat'.  How fat do you have to be to make the car scrape?<P>I might offend some people with this but did you know that North America has the most fat people in the world?<P>Can you say BIG MAC?<P>Now, before you start flamin' me to a crisp, I DO realize some are genetic disorders.  <P>Only SOME.<P>Regardless of the above, I don't like bumper stickers and think this one may have been inappropriate.<P>Changing the subject slightly, recently I've seen a biker in front of me with a T-shirt that said: 'If you can read this, the bi*ch fell off'.  Again, someone will say it's probably offensive to women, but definitely funny.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
